\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Where this work sits among systems that steer a synthetic-data budget. \emph  {Acquisition signal} is what decides where the budget goes; \emph  {generator control} is what the method can actually vary in the generated image; \emph  {diversity control} is what stops the budget piling onto near-duplicates; \emph  {closed-loop} means the downstream model's state feeds back into generation; \emph  {abstention/control} is whether a signal-destroying or same-shape control is run, which is what separates an effect of aiming from an effect of concentrating. The last column is the one this paper argues is missing from the literature, not a claim of superiority --- our own entry records a null.}}{15}{table.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:closest}{{4}{15}{Where this work sits among systems that steer a synthetic-data budget. \emph {Acquisition signal} is what decides where the budget goes; \emph {generator control} is what the method can actually vary in the generated image; \emph {diversity control} is what stops the budget piling onto near-duplicates; \emph {closed-loop} means the downstream model's state feeds back into generation; \emph {abstention/control} is whether a signal-destroying or same-shape control is run, which is what separates an effect of aiming from an effect of concentrating. The last column is the one this paper argues is missing from the literature, not a claim of superiority --- our own entry records a null}{table.4}{}}
